.TH "YAMLR-REPORT-ISSUE" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-report-issue \- Propose repairs and remediate Kubernetes manifests.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBUpload redacted local forensic logs for analysis.\fR
.PP
The \fBreport-issue\fR command allows you to share diagnostic data with the Yamlr support team while ensuring your sensitive information remains private.
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr report-issue [options]
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
This command performs a multi-stage redaction of your local logs and environment data before uploading a forensic bundle to our secure support endpoint.
.PP
\fBAutomatic Redaction includes:\fR
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Absolute system paths (HOME, TMP, CWD)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Sensitive environment variables (Secrets, Tokens)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Kubernetes manifest content (unless explicitly authorized)
.SH "OPTIONS"
| Flag | Description |
.PP
|:--|:--|
.PP
| \fB--bundle PATH\fR | Path to a pre-generated diagnostic bundle (from \fByamlr diagnose --bundle\fR) |
.PP
| \fB--comment TEXT\fR | Add a human description to the report |
.PP
| \fB--no-upload\fR | Redact and package the bundle locally without uploading |
.PP
.SH "STRATEGIC VALUE"
1. \fBEnterprise Supportability\fR: Enables rapid resolution of complex environmental issues without compromising security.
.PP
2. \fBZero-PII Compliance\fR: Built-in redaction engine ensures that your forensic data complies with SOC2 and GDPR requirements.
.PP
---
.PP
* Use \fByamlr diagnose --bundle\fR first to generate a diagnostic package.*
.PP
